{
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A leak is just a pipe you cannot see.\n\nIf a pump should fill a tank in 4 hours but actually takes 5 hours, some of the incoming water is escaping.\n\nThe leak rate is the missing part between the normal rate and the slower real rate.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A pump fills a tank in 4 hours, so its normal rate is 1/4 tank/hour. With a leak, the tank fills in 5 hours, so the actual net rate is 1/5.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Leak rate = 1/4 − 1/5 = 1/20 tank/hour.\nSo the leak alone would empty the full tank in 20 hours.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
